  Sensible (aka Lazydeb) — Debian Testing Live Installer

  The installer starts automatically and checks the Internet connection
  before it offers any disk. Network setup is guided if needed.
  To start it by hand, run:
    sensible-install   (or: lazydeb)

  Sensible installs a UEFI-only system; a BIOS-booted session is refused.

  To configure the network manually from the shell:
    nmtui   (or: nmcli device wifi connect <SSID> password <PASS>)
